    "physical_description": "Round box with a globular knob mounted on a dome-shaped cover. They are made of wood with decorations painted in black lacquer. Embellished on the outside of the box are flowering branches and a folding fan with Chinese inscription; while a Chinese mythical lion (<i>qilin</i>), a handscroll with Chinese inscription and flowering branches are depicting on the cover. Both the knob and rims are covered with silver under a layer of transparent red-tinted lacquer that gives silver a gold appearance. On the inside, the box is covered with an opaque red lacquer (vermilion).",
    "summary": "This box, embellished with Chinese-style designs in black lacquer under a transparent red-tinted lacquer, shows one of the two distinctive techniques used in Palembang lacquerware. The lacquer may have been dyed with ‘Dragon's blood’, a bright red resin obtained from the fruit of indigenous palms of the genus <i>Daemonorops</i>. Palembang has a long history of producing high quality ‘Dragon’s blood’ and exporting it to China for use in the lacquer industry.",
